From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:40:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Eden (Doris): real GPU barriers on Adreno (setting, on by
 default)

Eden turns the game's wait-for-idle into vkCmdSetEvent + vkCmdWaitEvents with TOP_OF_PIPE as the
destination and no memory barrier, which gives neither ordering nor visibility, and puts no barrier
after compute dispatches. On Adreno (Turnip and Qualcomm) later draws can then read culling results,
indirect arguments and vertex data that are not finished yet, so things drop out for a frame.

- doris_gpu_barriers 1 (default): wait-for-idle is a full memory barrier; every dispatch is followed
  by a compute -> all-commands barrier
- 2: also turns the game's tiled-cache barriers (a no-op in Eden) into full barriers
- 0: Eden's behaviour, for comparison
